{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"foliated-correct-arcticfox","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nOn `origin/main` at `25d1d683e55a`, `make worktree name=comment-remediation-3e32` selected `/opt/homebrew/bin/uv` 0.12.9 while `pyproject.toml` requires 0.12.7. `uv venv` correctly refused the mismatch, but the Makefile catch-all handler reported that Python 3.12 was unavailable and advised `uv python install 3.12`. Running the same target with the existing 0.12.7 binary created a Python 3.12.13 venv, proving that diagnosis false.\n\nThe exact uv pin and its refusal are intentional. This bug is the misleading classification of every `uv venv` failure as a missing interpreter. It is distinct from `princely-courageous-milksnake`, which repairs the machine-local updater uv selection.\n\n## Approach\nKeep fail-fast provisioning. Add a preflight that compares the selected uv executable/version with the repository exact required version before `uv venv`, and emit a mismatch-specific diagnostic naming the executable, actual version, and required version. Preserve the existing interpreter-unavailable diagnostic for a compatible uv whose venv operation fails.\n\nExtend the real-Makefile subprocess tests with controlled uv stubs for both failure classes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A selected uv version that violates `[tool.uv].required-version` fails before provisioning and names the selected path, actual version, and required version.\n- [ ] The mismatch path does not claim Python is unavailable or advise installing the already-available pinned interpreter.\n- [ ] A compatible uv whose `uv venv --python <pin>` fails still reports the pinned-interpreter provisioning failure.\n- [ ] `make worktree` continues to propagate either provisioning failure without printing its success message.\n- [ ] Focused Makefile worktree/python-pin tests, lint, and typecheck pass.","id":"1f58-ba19-afac-445e","parent_id":"","priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["devex","makefile","diagnostics","uv"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"make worktree misreports a uv version mismatch as a missing Python interpreter"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788584510722419001,"uuid":"0ee255b5-7779-4b78-9387-a939f0a7b19f"}